1788991607277190	sigil-dev	itc:v3:AWLOeSZkkyTnmRAAAAAAQd3q2q1d7QAAAAExAQ		item.create	bn-2h0a	{"description":"Observed in Sigil cr-1kz2vg after Maw recovery restored the complete valid Seal event log. seal sync --accept-regression cr-1kz2vg warns ReviewRetargeted does not match projected review target or status. SyncService::accept_regression deletes only file state and replays stateful retarget events onto an advanced projection. Exact restored log replays cleanly in fresh isolated projection, current approved7403a479 and merged54ac0e74. Avoid global rebuild because unrelated missing reviews have preserved projection data. Need targeted atomic reset/replay of one review preserving all other reviews. Source crates/seal-core/src/core/sync.rs:48. Evidence /home/bob/src/sigil/target/grpc-host-api-13.NSUGuNcA and /tmp/sigil-seal-record-verify.NZpKzsYs. No Seal source edits or global rebuild.","kind":"bug","labels":["projection"],"size":"m","title":"Make targeted regression sync rebuild one retargeted review"}	blake3:_Jy1ap6PrhKoKsxG_SiC_kzxPLADPhPUXBQkT4VLnQU
1790194517347795	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.create	bn-rk34	{"description":"# Problem\nThe LGTM vote writes .seal/reviews/<id>/events.jsonl in the workspace. .seal/.gitignore ignores only index.db, so review logs are meant to be tracked. But committing the review log is itself a commit after the approval. `seal reviews mark-merged` then exits 1 (\"the approval does not cover the current code\"), and `seal diff` reports approval_stale. So the documented rule \"commit nothing after the LGTM\" cannot hold together with tracking reviews in the repo.\n\nObserved in ~/src/continuum on 2026-09-23. The user expects: create a maw workspace, do the work, review it, commit the changes AND the review in the workspace, then merge. Every merge that way needs --allow-stale-approval plus a written justification, even though the extra commit changes no reviewed code. The same applies to any post-LGTM commit that touches only .seal/ (for example a reply or a resolved thread).\n\n# Proposed fix\nIn the staleness computation (mark-merged, seal diff approval_stale/uncovered_commits, and any merge gate), ignore commits whose changes are confined to .seal/. An approval then stays fresh across \"chore: seal review <id>\" commits. Any commit touching a path outside .seal/, even a mixed one, still makes the approval stale.\n\n# Acceptance\n- LGTM at commit A, then commit only .seal/reviews/<id>: mark-merged succeeds and seal diff reports approval_stale=false.\n- LGTM at A, then a commit touching .seal/ and one source file: still stale.\n- Tests cover both, plus a commit that deletes or renames under .seal/.\n\nRelated: edict bn-2f92 (the workflow docs never commit Seal review logs).","kind":"bug","title":"Staleness check should ignore commits that touch only .seal/ (committing the review log makes the LGTM stale)"}	blake3:IJ0NcAeABonGwqSScFyEwa8j5yRc6n15Uxr5NKGxibw
1790194517451367	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAg		item.create	bn-jnp9	{"description":"# Problem\n`seal reviews create` stores the branch's fork point as base_commit, and later commits extend the range. After `maw ws sync` rebases the workspace onto a newer trunk, `seal reviews retarget <id>` moves the target to the new head but keeps the OLD base_commit. The old base is no longer an ancestor boundary of the rebased branch, so the review range (seal diff, and what a reviewer is asked to review) now includes unrelated trunk commits merged since the original fork point.\n\nObserved in ~/src/continuum on 2026-09-23 with review cr-35xovl. After a rebase and retarget, the review kept base 2005cde while `git merge-base HEAD main` was 0727196, so the range grew to 19 commits, 16 of them unrelated trunk commits. The workaround was to abandon the review and create a new one after every rebase. That loses the review's threads and vote history, and it is why several reviews there show as abandoned (cr-35xovl, cr-2n0xng, cr-106znn, cr-3mpzmh).\n\n# Proposed fix\nEither:\n- retarget detects that base_commit is no longer an ancestor boundary of the new target and re-derives it as merge-base(target, trunk), recording the old and new base in the event log; or\n- retarget gains an explicit --rebase-base (or --base <rev>) option, and seal diff warns when base_commit is not an ancestor of the target.\nThreads anchored to lines should be re-mapped or flagged as outdated, not dropped.\n\n# Acceptance\n- Create a review, rebase the workspace onto a newer trunk, retarget: the range is exactly the workspace's own commits, with the same commit count as before the rebase.\n- The event log records the base change, and the prior vote is cleared as it is today.\n- A test covers rebase-then-retarget, and the warning when the base is not an ancestor.","kind":"bug","title":"retarget keeps the pre-rebase base_commit, so after maw ws sync the review range includes unrelated trunk commits"}	blake3:gt5jOmZiY-M_osjb54Jl-4MjujqJ6JBiWaqrHE-Ql6E
1790470001474845	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1i54	{"description":"Add machine-checked properties where seal has a history of bugs. Tools: Kani (installed) for bounded pure functions, proptest for differential and model-based checks. No Verus: every candidate property decomposes per step. Every proof or property must be shown non-vacuous by a deliberate mutation that turns it red.","kind":"goal","labels":["verification"],"title":"Formal verification and property testing for seal"}	blake3:IykSJ0BbAyHDAYwXHeobRZR29qmgyPy2BQOsJJORYhM
1790470001583569	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2nu3	{"description":"Add proptest as a seal-core dev-dependency. Declare cfg(kani) in check-cfg so clippy -D warnings stays clean. Add a Justfile recipe 'kani' that runs cargo kani -p seal-core. Prerequisite for the other verification bones, done first to avoid Cargo.toml conflicts.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-1i54","size":"s","title":"Verification tooling: proptest dev-dep, cfg(kani) lint, just kani recipe"}	blake3:pPbbGqyJgp4SwIdxV_o6wue5rpbBsLSDBXh15nUKPns
1790470001692542	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-fx8g	{"description":"jj/drift.rs calculate_drift uses unchecked u32 math: old_start + old_count - 1 and current_line += new_lines - old_lines. A header like '@@ -4294967295,2 +1,1 @@' parses, then panics (debug) or wraps (release). Extract the per-hunk shift arithmetic into a pure fn, make it checked/saturating, prove with Kani: no overflow, result in bounds. Also Kani-prove log/mod.rs validate_review_id: accepted ID contains no '/', '\\\\', '..', NUL, is non-empty. Add proptest: drift preserves order of surviving lines. Mutation-check each harness.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-1i54","size":"s","title":"Kani: prove calculate_drift hunk arithmetic and validate_review_id"}	blake3:HiBcwi3YnUGVqb1dFxzg2tVFoLQ2N075Cv3dX9EYsYI
1790470001803459	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2n88	{"description":"History: bd-1s1 (empty lines), bd-oum (same-length replacement), bd-2ji (hasher), 1ee4902 (cursor). Properties: for any log L and appended events E, prefix_hash(L++E, lines(L)) == prefix_hash(L, lines(L)); any non-append edit of the first N lines changes prefix_hash(N) or line count; blank and trailing lines do not shift the cursor. Mutation-check.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-1i54","size":"s","title":"proptest: log prefix_hash and sync cursor are stable under append"}	blake3:1lzNJNmXAXp5eDfKUscA4FWzPLX5I0-TXeo2LHXg2QU
1790470001914748	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2a4t	{"description":"The projection reducer lives in SQL (projection/mod.rs apply_*), so no tool can see it. Add a pure in-memory model (projection/model.rs, test-only or cfg(test)) with apply(state, event) -> Result<state>, mirroring the SQL semantics. proptest: generated event sequences over a few reviews/threads, SQL projection == pure fold. Then Kani/proptest frame condition: an event for review R never changes other reviews. Supports bn-2h0a.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-1i54","size":"m","title":"Pure review reducer oracle + differential proptest against SQL projection"}	blake3:M1BKosK83S_I_MRdElLbGNZMr1ds9cw54anJXIPX82I
