1790470020135178	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2h0a	{"body":"Root cause (read, not yet reproduced): accept_regression replays the full log onto existing rows. apply_review_retargeted guards on scm_anchor = old_scm_anchor, so a second apply matches 0 rows and bails. Fix: in one transaction delete all projected rows for the review (reviews, reviewer_votes, review_reviewers, threads, comments of its threads), then replay. Oracle test: targeted rebuild of R == fresh projection of R's log; other reviews' rows byte-identical."}	blake3:xaSry3y0Y6VP2V0MF2JMfUoq8WInnKFGbS4ne_5bBD0
1790470020154162	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-rk34	{"body":"Verification scope: stale = any uncovered commit touches a non-exempt path, so correctness reduces to the per-commit path classifier. Kani-prove the classifier. Traps: '.sealignore' must not match a '.seal' string prefix, renames need both sides exempt, '.seal' as a file, merge commits. Security: prefer the narrow rule, exempt only changes under .seal/ that cannot rewrite review history; consider requiring append-only for existing events.jsonl."}	blake3:PDAfMehcvWPBu37L8HuW0jm_5UhR8QytDOm7RztsbAM
1790470020169380	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-jnp9	{"body":"Missing invariant: retarget checks is_ancestor(base, new_target) (core/reviews.rs:251), which still holds after rebase. Needed: no commit in base..target is reachable from trunk. Test with a model-based sequence (trunk_commit, ws_commit, rebase, retarget) on real temp git repos; oracle: range == the workspace's own commits."}	blake3:AQcX6qKHcAwH3yQ051EP5vyChKv0hVRlCo7UEdSJFic
