1790470546113491	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-jnp9	{"body":"Related, observed 2026-09-26 in seal itself: in a maw workspace, discover_base_commit chose origin/main (33f22b8), which lagged local main by 4 unpushed commits, so a new review covered 5 commits instead of 1. The trunk used for base re-derivation must be the local trunk (main), or the merge-base of the candidates nearest the target, not the first candidate that resolves. Cover both create and retarget."}	blake3:764tkF0DbpA78z0PQJkav2W4AbVvosVD3uVVu4et2rE
1790470546217147	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-7uli	{"description":"Found during bn-2h0a. When review_file_state has no rows, sync_from_review_logs takes its bootstrap path (Step 1b): it re-seeds file state from disk and replays nothing. If projected reviews exist but their logs changed, the change goes undetected. bn-2h0a avoids this on the accept-regression path by writing the file state before syncing. Check whether any normal flow can empty review_file_state while reviews stay projected (schema migration, manual delete, older versions) and either replay or detect in that case. Add a test that fails first.","kind":"bug","labels":["projection"],"parent":"bn-1i54","size":"s","title":"Sync bootstrap path replays nothing when review_file_state is empty but reviews are projected"}	blake3:EUx4jqyq2BoSNf-bcJ-391LGIQVtLD0TgpvvCGLZX_Q
