1790473394500264	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3rk0	{"description":"From bn-rk34. In jj, committing the review log amends @, which rewrites the approved commit, so approved_commit is no longer an ancestor of the target and approval_coverage returns stale before the .seal/ exemption runs. The tree comparison in approval_exempt.rs is sound without the ancestor check: if tree(A) and tree(T) differ only in exempt .seal/ changes, the merged code equals the approved code. Consider running the exemption check for non-descendant targets too. Keep the NoApprovedCommit case stale. Add a jj test.","kind":"task","labels":["verification"],"parent":"bn-1i54","size":"s","title":"jj: approval stays stale after writing the review log into the approved change"}	blake3:OG5Mxf5CTnEK_mi1Z_m5YBeboWKNnk2cZL7DKcSmuLQ
