1790475311939162	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2otl	{"description":"From bn-jnp9 acceptance: threads anchored to lines should be re-mapped or flagged as outdated after a rebase and retarget, not dropped. Threads store commit_hash + line; jj/drift.rs calculate_drift maps a line from the thread's commit to the current one. After a rebase the thread's commit is no longer an ancestor of the target and the diff between them includes unrelated trunk changes. First establish current behaviour with a real git test (thread on line N of a feature file, trunk edits the same file above and elsewhere, rebase, retarget): what do seal review / seal threads / seal diff show? Fix whatever drops or mis-places threads; outdated threads must stay visible, marked outdated.","kind":"bug","labels":["retarget"],"size":"m","title":"Line-anchored threads after rebase + retarget: verify re-mapping, flag outdated instead of dropping"}	blake3:t_BnzDu62mVQROsoh9mvJihwVyqkGxt-aNyp-QosX7U
1790475312092469	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2r6t	{"description":"From bn-jnp9. Reviews created before ranges were supported have base_commit NULL. retarget requires the new target to descend from the OLD TARGET for them, so after a rebase it errors, and rederive_base never runs. Fix: when the review has no persisted base, derive one with discover_base_commit(new_target) (fall back to today's behaviour when discovery finds nothing), record it as new_base_commit in ReviewRetargeted, and keep all other checks. Update projection/model.rs if semantics change. Test with a real git repo.","kind":"bug","labels":["retarget"],"size":"s","title":"Retarget of a legacy review with no persisted base cannot follow a rebase"}	blake3:TQFhrtaQtKUoASpohf1M5rBSWrJHe3uSx3JLPAeiW-w
1790475312232852	seal-aask1l	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-y7nm	{"description":"From bn-jnp9. is_own_remote_copy excludes origin/feature for feature, but a local branch tracking its own remote copy under another name (feature -> origin/feature-v2) still counts as a trunk candidate, so the base can move past pushed feature commits. Rare setup. Possible rule: an upstream is a trunk candidate only if the current branch is not the only branch whose history contains its tip, or only if it matches a configured trunk name.","kind":"bug","labels":["retarget"],"size":"xs","title":"Base discovery treats a branch's own remote copy under a different name as trunk","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:NgGhov4vzO552TuqHT8P8IuC0OYvn05bQo0boV6BxKk
