1790555727108288	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3j7p	{"description":"Filed from edict (goal bn-30a0: the edict-managed AGENTS.md section will point agents at seal's own help). Found by edict's audit (edict repo: notes/managed-trim-audit.md). `seal agents show`:\n\n1. Runs `seal` directly; in maw projects reviews live in the workspace, so the commands must run as `maw exec <ws> -- seal ...`.\n2. Offers `seal reviews mark-merged --self-approve` without saying when (if ever) that is acceptable.\n3. Lists mark-merged last with no ordering against the merge. Correct order in maw projects: mark-merged while HEAD is still the approved commit, commit `.seal/reviews/<id>` in the workspace, then merge (the merge destroys the workspace).\n4. Still refers to jj change IDs and `--json` (current flag: `--format json`).\n5. Does not mention `seal reviews retarget` before re-requesting after new commits.\n\nAcceptance: `seal agents show` matches current flags and the git+maw workflow, and every example runs as written.","kind":"task","labels":["docs"],"size":"s","title":"seal agents show is out of date: direct seal calls, --self-approve, mark-merged ordering, jj ids, --json"}	blake3:fRY9z3kBLiA0sXMmeEHJeFu-aDv-f7TB6sDIgIZVR2w
1790557081017590	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ypz	{"description":"Filed from edict (found by edict's eval harness, bn-1oug). maw workspaces are git worktrees on a detached HEAD. After an LGTM, a new code commit in the workspace should make `seal diff <id> --format json` report `approval_stale: true` (with `uncovered_commits`) and make `seal reviews mark-merged` exit 1 ('the approval does not cover the current code'). With seal 0.30 on a detached HEAD, approval_stale stayed false and mark-merged accepted the new commit. Edict's merge gate and the 'no code after the LGTM' rule depend on this detection.\n\nRepro: maw ws create w --from main; commit; seal reviews create; lgtm; commit another change in the workspace; `maw exec w -- seal diff <id> --format json` and `mark-merged`. Acceptance: stale detection works on a detached HEAD, with a test.","kind":"bug","size":"s","title":"approval_stale is false and mark-merged accepts a post-LGTM commit on a detached HEAD (maw workspaces)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:FQtHnvF71bYL-XNftfh4S_FOHYoN4GiXKwJPws3BjiY
1790557661469647	edict-83n310	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ypz	{"body":"Confirmed repro (seal 0.30.0, maw 1.0.0-pre.16, sandbox): after LGTM, a new commit in the maw workspace (detached HEAD) leaves 'seal diff <id> --format json' byte-identical: approval_stale:false, approved_commit == target_commit == old commit, uncovered_commits:0. 'seal reviews mark-merged' then exits 0 with final_commit = the new unreviewed HEAD. approved_commit itself is correct; approval_stale and uncovered_commits are wrong. Edict now cross-checks approved_commit against HEAD (edict bn-2cyu)."}	blake3:posnfl5iSUQB6z8S9uFkwhrft_oIHAeWlw7saHJkrYw
